id: pm-0vqbl5
title: Give recurrence policy globs a deterministic matching bound
description: "Replace recurrence file-pattern regex execution with a bounded wildcard matcher while preserving the published policy grammar, Unicode handling and existing path semantics. Keep SDK consumers free to supply custom project policy without an implicit regex execution cost."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: improve,performance,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-13T05:47:55.612Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T08:39:45.253Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T08:39:44.221Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T08:39:44.221Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Literal regex punctuation stays literal; single and double stars retain their separator and line-break behavior; Unicode paths and empty patterns remain compatible; repeated wildcard matching has a deterministic bound; full SDK and runtime gates pass.
parent: pm-oz8u
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Replace dynamic path-pattern regex execution with cached wildcard tokens and two bounded state rows, preserving the published literal, Unicode, separator and line-terminator grammar."
expected_result: Matching costs at most pattern length times path length and uses memory proportional to the bounded pattern size.
actual_result: "26 public SDK cases pass, including 18 independent compatibility cases and long repeated-wildcard paths; full coverage is exact 100/100/100/100 and final packed Node/Bun/npx/bunx workflows preserve artifact budgets."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
